## 5. Variable Groups (ADO Library)

Create these Variable Groups in **ADO → Pipelines → Library** before registering any pipeline.

### `vg-pa-tools`
| Variable Name                          | Example Value                                                                           | Secret |
|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------|
| `PC_LINT_PLUS_DIR_PATH`               | `D:\tools\PCLint\pclp`                                                                  | No     |
| `VISUAL_STUDIO_VCVARS_BAT_FULL_PATH`  | `D:\tools\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Professional\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvars64.bat`    | No     |
| `ANT_HOME`                             | `D:\tools\apache-ant-1.10.x`                                                            | No     |
| `JAVA_HOME`                            | `D:\tools\jdk`                                                                          | No     |

### `vg-pa-build`
| Variable Name          | Example Value | Description                  |
|------------------------|---------------|------------------------------|
| `PROJECT_BUILDTYPE`    | `Release`     | MSBuild configuration        |
| `BOOSTTEST_LOG_LEVEL`  | `all`         | Boost.Test verbosity         |

### `vg-pa-svn`
| Variable Name               | Example Value                        | Secret |
|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------|--------|
| `SVN_ARTEFACTS_URL`        | `https://svn.example.com/artefacts`  | No     |
| `SVN_USERNAME`              | `svc-build`                          | No     |
| `SVN_PASSWORD`              | `***`                                | Yes    |

> **Note:** If migrating from SVN to Git, the `vg-pa-svn` group and all SVN-related steps can be removed. ADO will handle source checkout natively.

