## 7. Migration Steps

### Phase 1 — Preparation (no code changes)
- [ ] Create ADO Variable Groups (`vg-pa-tools`, `vg-pa-build`, `vg-pa-svn`)
- [ ] Set up self-hosted Windows agent pool (`pa-windows-build-agents`)
- [ ] Install and verify all required tools on agent machine(s)
- [ ] Ensure SVN checkout / Git clone works on the agent
- [ ] Copy `pipelines/` folder from this doc into repository root (or a `/.azuredevops/` folder)

### Phase 2 — Register pipelines one by one
1. **`ci.yml`** — Register first. Verify cmake + msbuild work end-to-end.
2. **`ci-unittest.yml`** — Add unit test stage. Verify XML reports are published.
3. **`lint.yml`** — Verify PC-lint Plus runs and reports are attached.
4. **`lint-misc-components.yml`** — Mirror of lint for misc components.
5. **`nightly.yml`** — Full nightly last (most complex; includes SVN commit).

### Phase 3 — Trigger policies
- Set **branch policies** on `main`/`trunk` to require `ci.yml` to pass before merge.
- Schedule `nightly.yml` with a **cron trigger** (e.g. `0 22 * * 1-5` = weekdays 22:00).
- Schedule `lint.yml` once or twice per week.

### Phase 4 — Cleanup (optional)
- Remove Ant/Jenkins job definitions from old build server.
- Remove `setup.properties` / `local.properties` references and replace with ADO variable groups entirely.

