## 9. Test Results & Lint Reports in ADO

### Unit Test Results
Boost.Test writes XML in JUnit format (`--log_format=XML`).
ADO can publish and display this natively.

In each pipeline, after running tests, add:
```yaml
- task: PublishTestResults@2
  inputs:
    testResultsFormat: JUnit
    testResultsFiles: 'log/*.Test.xml'
    mergeTestResults: true
    testRunTitle: 'Unit Tests - $(Build.BuildNumber)'
  condition: always()   # publish even if tests failed
```

Result: visible as the **Tests** tab on every pipeline run in ADO.

### PC-lint Plus Reports
PC-lint Plus writes results to `construct/LintResults/`.
Publish as pipeline artifacts so they are downloadable from the ADO run page:
```yaml
- task: PublishBuildArtifacts@1
  inputs:
    pathToPublish: '$(CONSTRUCT_DIR)/LintResults'
    artifactName: 'LintResults'
  condition: always()
```

> **Optional enhancement:** Use the [Warnings Next Generation plugin] pattern — convert PC-lint output to a format that ADO Extensions (e.g. "SARIF SAST Scans Tab") can display inline in the UI.

